fix(core): probe engine synchronously; parse /health model strings

Three bugs found by running the release binary end-to-end:

- startup probe was async, so --status and the first chat request could see
  backend=none just after launch. Probe now completes before start() returns,
  with a 15s background recheck for late-starting engines.
- /health returns models as ["a","b"] but the client parsed only
  /v1/models-style [{"id":"a"}]. Zero models were reported while the
  endpoint was correct. Parser now accepts both shapes, with a regression test.
- chat with no backend attempted 127.0.0.1:8080 and reported a confusing 502.
  Now returns 503 with an actionable message. Discovery port conflicts are
  silent unless PRIVATELM_DEBUG is set.

verified: --status lists models, --once streams a real reply
